From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: plain macro DMA reads on pages the GPU never wrote skip the drain (d3zessete, Frizti/Fritchii PR #35), off by default; EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN counter line

Switches: EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN_FAST=1 (exact 1, a live switch, Id DmaUnwrittenFast, not armed).
EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN_FAST_VERIFY=1 (exact 1, read once at the first fast read). Counter line:
with EDEN_UP_DMA_MISS_STATS=1 (0573) or EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN_FAST=1.

What: PR #35 lets the split front's FrontDmaRead skip its drain, the buffer flush and the query
flush when no page it reads may be GPU-written and no 3D report write to it is still queued. In
our tree that idea already exists for DMA snapshot misses: EDEN_UP_L1028_DMA_WAIT (0485, zortos293
Lichii #1028) waits for the queued work that may write the pages, then reads guest memory when the
pages hold no GPU writes and the query cache lists no report. So this port covers only what
neither the snapshot nor L1028 reaches: the plain drained path at the end of FrontDmaRead (no DMA
snapshot or its off phase, reads into the MME data RAM, reads of listed reports, reads the snapshot
cannot take). There, with the switch on: mapped in one piece (every page, IsContinuousRange),
no query DMA trace, no EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_SYNC, no page ever GPU-written
(VideoCore::MayHoldGpuWrites: Switch 2 titles only, ranges past the page bitmap count as written),
then GpuSplit::WaitForNotedWriters over the
pages (compute, copies, unranged writers, noted writes such as the 3D reports), then the same page
check again and no listed report (HasCachedReports, 12 bytes back as the snapshot does): the read
takes guest memory without the Defer and the drain. Otherwise the old path, counted as a fall-back.
Differences from the PR, all to the safe side: the wait is L1028's (it also covers unranged writers
and every noted write, the PR waited for compute and copies only and then looked up its own report
slot map); listed reports keep the drain (the PR's own open point: "not verified that reports held
in the query cache always land on pages marked GPU-written"); not on other titles (the bitmap is
only filled for Switch 2 titles; the PR did not check); no report slot map (it was never pruned).

EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN (the counter line, about every 10 s while reads come, front thread only):
"EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN: <s> s of front DMA reads, on pages the GPU never wrote with no listed
report / all: snapshot hit a/A, L1028 narrowed b/B, snapshot miss drained c/C, plain drained d/D,
read ahead e/E; EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN_FAST skipped the drain of f (g fell back after its wait),
verify h checked i differed". d of D is an upper estimate of what EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN_FAST
could take (counted before its wait and its second check). c of C is the snapshot misses on
never-written pages; EDEN_UP_L1028_DMA_WAIT may take more than c (it also narrows marked pages
the buffer cache holds no GPU writes for), so c is no bound on what it can win. With _VERIFY=1 the
f fast reads drained anyway. With only EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN_FAST on, only the plain path is
counted.

Off (both unset): one live-switch load in the plain drained path; snapshot hits, misses and the
read-ahead path never look at it. With EDEN_UP_DMA_MISS_STATS off, nothing is counted. Changes no
shader translation and no shader-store stamp: the names are in common/live_switch.h and
video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp only, outside the sources TranslationSwitches is made from.

Risk when on: a page the GPU writes without a mark, or a draw that writes it while still queued
(the snapshot and L1028 trust the same notes), gives the macro old words: a wrong occlusion or
draw count, seen as a flash, a missing or extra object for a frame. EDEN_UP_DMA_UNWRITTEN_FAST_VERIFY=1
drains anyway, compares, logs the first 32 differences and gives the macro the drained words.

Review (T150): the fast path's read now needs every page mapped in one run
(MemoryManager::IsContinuousRange), not only matching first and last bytes: the page check is on
device addresses, the read on GPU addresses. The one case the wait cannot see: draws are no noted
writers, so a draw still queued that is the first GPU write ever to a page (shader stores, transform
feedback) is not waited for; its page is marked only when the back records it. Marks never clear, so
this is the first write of a page only, and the snapshot hits and L1028 trust the same notes. The
MME data RAM is the front's alone in split mode (macro.cpp: a call the back runs gets its own), so
skipping the drain for data RAM reads changes no order there.

Origin and credit: d3zessete, Frizti/Fritchii PR #35 "Fast-path DMA reads on pages not written by
the GPU" (open, not merged; head 23b88f1c2b), on Fritchii's split front. The page bitmap is
zortos293/Lichii #463's, the wait zortos293/Lichii #1028's (0485). Port, names and counter ours.
---
diff --git a/src/common/live_switch.h b/src/common/live_switch.h
index 1cce34c..156b0a3 100644
--- a/src/common/live_switch.h
